Let me look at the `secondline_is_bases` function again. Actually, let me reconsider. The issue is a heap-buffer-overflow READ 1. Let me look at the `parse_tabbed_text` function more carefully.

Actually, let me look at the `colmatch` function:

```c
static int colmatch(const char *columns, const char *pattern)
{
    int i;
    for (i = 0; columns[i] != '\0'; i++) {
        if (pattern[i] == '+') return i;
        if (! (columns[i] == pattern[i] || pattern[i] == 'Z')) return 0;
    }
    return i;
}
```

This reads `pattern[i]` where `i` goes up to `strlen(columns)`. The pattern strings are constants like `"ZiZiiCZiiZZOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO+"`. If `columns` is longer than the pattern, then `pattern[i]` would read past the end of the pattern string. But `columns` is at most 23 chars (column_len=24, so ncolumns up to 23). The pattern `"ZiZiiCZiiZZOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO+"` is longer than 23. So that's fine.

